## Testing Standards

### Philosophy: Specification by Example / Living Documentation

Tests serve as executable specifications. Every test traces back to a **Specification > User Story > Scenario > User Acceptance Criterion (UAC)**. Feature files provide human-readable documentation; test classes provide executable verification.

### Traceability Constants

The `Spec` static class defines trait keys for xUnit filtering:

```csharp
public static class Spec
{
    public const string SPEC = "SPEC";
    public const string US = "US";
    public const string SC = "SC";
    public const string UAC = "UAC";
}
```

Every test is uniquely identified by a 4-level hierarchy:

```
SPEC0623.US01.SC01.UAC01
|        |    |    +-- User Acceptance Criterion ID
|        |    +------- Scenario ID
|        +------------ User Story ID
+---------------------- Specification ID
```

### Folder Structure

```
src/test/
+-- Scenario.cs                          # Base class for all scenarios
+-- FakeContextFactory.cs                # In-memory DB factory (if needed)
+-- GlobalUsings.cs                      # Global using statements
|
+-- SPEC0623.PluginGenerator/            # Specification folder
|   +-- US01.CommandParsing/             # User Story folder
|   |   +-- US01.CommandParsing.feature  # Gherkin spec (living docs)
|   |   +-- SC01_ParseValidName.cs       # Scenario test class
|   |   +-- SC02_ParseInvalidName.cs
|   |   +-- SC03_ParseShellCommands.cs
|   |
|   +-- US02.PluginTemplateGeneration/
|   |   +-- US02.PluginTemplateGeneration.feature
|   |   +-- SC01_GeneratePluginCs.cs
|   |   +-- SC02_GenerateProjectFiles.cs
|   |   +-- SC03_GenerateSolutionFile.cs
|   |
|   +-- US03.PipelineExecution/
|   +-- US04.OutputValidation/
```

**Naming conventions:**
- Spec folders: `SPECXXXX.ComponentName/`
- User Story folders: `USXX.StoryName/`
- Feature files: `USXX.StoryName.feature`
- Scenario classes: `SCXX_ScenarioName.cs`

### Feature File Pattern (Gherkin)

```gherkin
@US01
Feature: US01 - Command Parsing

    @SC01
    Scenario: Parse valid plugin name with dot separator
        Given the command parser is initialized
        When I parse the input "MyOrg.MyPlugin"
        #UAC01
        Then the organization name should be "MyOrg"
        #UAC02
        And the plugin name should be "MyPlugin"

    @SC02
    Scenario: Parse invalid name without dot separator
        Given the command parser is initialized
        When I parse the input "InvalidName"
        #UAC03
        Then a validation exception should be thrown
        #UAC04
        And the error message should indicate the format is invalid
```

**UAC tagging rules (CRITICAL):**
1. `#UAC` tags go **immediately before** `Then` or `And` lines (assertions only)
2. **Never** place `#UAC` on `Given` or `When` lines (those are setup/action, not assertions)
3. Each assertion (`Then`/`And`) gets its own sequential UAC number
4. UAC numbering is **sequential across ALL scenarios** within a User Story
5. Never skip or duplicate UAC numbers within a User Story

### Base Scenario Class

All test scenarios extend a base class implementing `IAsyncLifetime`:

```csharp
public abstract class Scenario : IAsyncLifetime
{
    protected HttpClient Client = null!;

    public async ValueTask InitializeAsync()
    {
        // Setup HttpClient, DI, test infrastructure
    }

    public async ValueTask DisposeAsync()
    {
        // Teardown
    }

    protected virtual Task GivenAsync() => Task.CompletedTask;
    protected virtual Task WhenAsync() => Task.CompletedTask;

    protected async Task ArrangeAndActAsync()
    {
        await GivenAsync();
        await WhenAsync();
    }
}
```

### Test Class Pattern

```csharp
namespace LowlandTech.Factory.Tests.SPEC0623.PluginGenerator.US01.CommandParsing;

[Trait(Spec.SPEC, "0623")]
[Trait(Spec.US, "01")]
[Trait(Spec.SC, "01")]
public class SC01_ParseValidName : Scenario
{
    private PluginNameResult? _result;

    protected override Task GivenAsync()
    {
        // Setup - matches "Given" in feature file
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    protected override async Task WhenAsync()
    {
        // Action - matches "When" in feature file
        var parser = new PluginNameParser();
        var attempt = parser.TryParse("MyOrg.MyPlugin");
        if (attempt.IsValid)
            _result = attempt.Value;
    }

    [Fact(DisplayName = "Then the organization name should be \"MyOrg\"")]
    [Trait(Spec.UAC, "01")]
    public async Task UAC01_OrganizationShouldBeMyOrg()
    {
        await ArrangeAndActAsync();
        _result.ShouldNotBeNull();
        _result!.Org.ShouldBe("MyOrg");
    }

    [Fact(DisplayName = "And the plugin name should be \"MyPlugin\"")]
    [Trait(Spec.UAC, "02")]
    public async Task UAC02_PluginNameShouldBeMyPlugin()
    {
        await ArrangeAndActAsync();
        _result.ShouldNotBeNull();
        _result!.Plugin.ShouldBe("MyPlugin");
    }
}
```

**Mandatory rules:**
- **Class-level traits**: `SPEC`, `US`, `SC` — applied once per scenario class
- **Method-level traits**: `UAC` — applied per `[Fact]` method
- **DisplayName**: Must match the Gherkin `Then`/`And` statement **exactly**
- **Method name**: Always `UACXX_DescriptiveName`
- **One assertion per test**: Every `Then`/`And` = one `[Fact]`
- **All async Task**: Every test method MUST be `async Task`
- **Shouldly assertions**: Use `ShouldBe`, `ShouldNotBeNull`, `ShouldContain` (not FluentAssertions)

### Test Filtering

```bash
# Run all tests for a specification
dotnet test --filter "SPEC=0623"

# Run all tests for a User Story
dotnet test --filter "SPEC=0623&US=01"

# Run a specific scenario (all its UACs)
dotnet test --filter "SPEC=0623&US=01&SC=01"

# Run a specific acceptance criterion
dotnet test --filter "SPEC=0623&US=01&SC=01&UAC=01"
```

### Common Pitfalls

| Mistake | Why It's Wrong | Fix |
|---------|----------------|-----|
| UAC tag before `When` | Marks action, not assertion | Move after `When`, before `Then` |
| Missing UAC on `And` | Can't trace individual assertions | Add `#UAC` to every `And` |
| Duplicate SC tags | Multiple scenarios with same ID | Use unique SC01, SC02, SC03... |
| Missing SPEC trait | Can't filter by specification | Always add all 4 traits |
| Sync test methods | Causes test hangs | Make all tests `async Task` |
| Skipping scenarios | Incomplete test coverage | Implement all or defer entire US |
| Using FluentAssertions | Wrong assertion library | Use Shouldly (`ShouldBe`, not `Should().Be()`) |
| Multiple assertions per Fact | Violates one-assertion-per-test | Split into separate UAC methods |

### Theory for Scenario Outlines

When a scenario has multiple data variations, use `[Theory]` with `[InlineData]`:

```csharp
[Theory]
[InlineData("MyOrg.MyPlugin", "MyOrg", "MyPlugin")]
[InlineData("acme.product", "acme", "product")]
[InlineData("company.module-name", "company", "module-name")]
[Trait(Spec.UAC, "01")]
public async Task UAC01_ShouldParseOrgAndPlugin(string input, string expectedOrg, string expectedPlugin)
{
    // ...
}
```

### bUnit Component Tests

```csharp
using Bunit;
using Xunit;

public class MyComponentTests : BunitContext
{
    [Fact]
    public void Component_RendersCorrectly()
    {
        Services.AddSingleton<IMyService, MockMyService>();
        var cut = Render<MyComponent>();
        var element = cut.Find(".expected-class");
        Assert.NotNull(element);
    }
}
```

**Key bUnit selectors for our components:**
- Buttons: `.btn.btn-default`, `.btn.btn-destructive`
- Cards: `.card`, `.card-header`, `.card-content`
- Nav links: `.nav-link`, `.nav-link.active`
- Sidebar: `.sidebar`, `.sidebar-text`

### E2E Tests (Playwright + Reqnroll)

```gherkin
@baget @marketplace
Feature: BaGet Marketplace Integration

Scenario: Marketplace shows packages from BaGet feed
    Given BaGet server is running at "http://localhost:5000"
    When I navigate to the Marketplace page
    Then I should see "TestPlugin.Backend" in the package list
```

**Use `@ignore` tag for WIP features:**
```gherkin
@ignore @wip
Feature: Plugin Configuration
  # This feature is not yet implemented
```

